00:28:07.560 --> 00:28:08.760
compared to the I-frames?

00:28:08.760 --> 00:28:12.010
Because these do look
different from natural images.

00:28:12.010 --> 00:28:13.980
Yeah, good point.

00:28:13.980 --> 00:28:19.680
So the hyper parameters
which are used for encoding

00:28:19.680 --> 00:28:22.590
can be different and it
depends on the encoder.

00:28:22.590 --> 00:28:26.850
So actually, I mean, for
the residual frame itself,

00:28:26.850 --> 00:28:31.470
I believe the Huffman
coding, Huffman tables itself

00:28:31.470 --> 00:28:33.400
which are used are--

00:28:33.400 --> 00:28:35.400
I mean, the preset Huffman
tables which are used

00:28:35.400 --> 00:28:39.040
are slightly different
in this case.

00:28:39.040 --> 00:28:39.540
Yeah.

00:28:42.210 --> 00:28:45.480
I mean, the H.264 standard
actually only specifies

00:28:45.480 --> 00:28:48.748
the decoder so you will see
that different encoders,

00:28:48.748 --> 00:28:50.040
they can do whatever they want.

00:28:52.880 --> 00:28:53.380
Yeah.

